{"id":"mahabharata-7-079","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":79,"title":"एकोनाशीतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 79 · Arjuna and the Kaurava champions","summary":{"en":"The Kauravas, seeing the two Krishnas, rush at them. Arjuna blows Devadatta so that the whole earth resounds and checks the foe with hundreds of arrows.","kn":"ಕೌರವರು ಕೃಷ್ಣಾರ್ಜುನರನ್ನು ಕಂಡು ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ದೇವದತ್ತ ಊದಿ ಭೂಮಿ ಮೊಳಗುವಂತೆ ಮಾಡಿ ನೂರಾರು ಬಾಣಗಳಿಂದ ಶತ್ರುಗಳನ್ನು ತಡೆಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण और अर्जुन को देखकर कौरव उन पर टूट पड़ते हैं। अर्जुन देवदत्त शंख बजाते हैं जिससे सारी पृथ्वी गूँज उठती है, और सैकड़ों बाणों से शत्रुओं को रोकते हैं।","te":"కృష్ణార్జునులను చూసి కౌరవులు దూసుకువస్తారు; అర్జునుడు దేవదత్తాన్ని ఊదగా భూమి మార్మోగుతుంది, వందల బాణాలతో శత్రువులను ఆపుతాడు.","ta":"கண்ணனையும் அர்ஜுனனையும் கண்டு கௌரவர் பாய்கின்றனர்; அர்ஜுனன் தேவதத்தம் முழங்கப் பூமி அதிர, நூற்றுக்கணக்கான அம்புகளால் பகைவரைத் தடுக்கிறான்.","ml":"രണ്ട് കൃഷ്ണന്മാരെ കണ്ട കൗരവർ അവർക്കുനേരെ പാഞ്ഞടുക്കുന്നു. അർജുനൻ ദേവദത്തം മുഴക്കുന്നു; ഭൂമി മുഴുവൻ പ്രതിധ്വനിക്കുന്നു, നൂറുകണക്കിന് അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് ശത്രുവിനെ തടയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.79; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तावकास्तु समीक्ष्यैव वृष्ण्यन्धककुरूत्तमौ ।\nप्रागत्वरञ्जिघांसन्तस्तथैव विजयः परान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the best of the Vrishnis and Andhakas and the best of the Kurus, your men hurried first, eager to kill them; and Arjuna likewise hurried at his foes."}},{"n":2,"text":"सुवर्णचित्रैर्वैयाघ्रैः स्वनवद्भिर्महारथैः ।\nदीपयन्तो दिशः सर्वा ज्वलद्भिरिव पावकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With great chariots bright with golden tiger-skins and rumbling, they lit up all the quarters as if with blazing fires,"}},{"n":3,"text":"रुक्मपृष्ठैश्च दुष्प्रेक्ष्यैः कार्मुकैः पृथिवीपते ।\nकूजद्भिरतुलान्नादान्रोषितैरुरगैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"and with gold-backed bows hard to look at, which twanged with matchless sounds like angered serpents."}},{"n":4,"text":"भूरिश्रवाः शलः कर्णो वृषसेनो जयद्रथः ।\nकृपश्च मद्रराजश्च द्रौणिश्च रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, Shala, Karna, Vrishasena, Jayadratha, Kripa, the king of Madras and Drona's son, best of charioteers,"}},{"n":5,"text":"ते पिबन्त इवाकाशमश्वैरष्टौ महारथाः ।\nव्यराजयन्दश दिशो वैयाघ्रैर्हेमचन्द्रकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those eight great chariot-warriors, as if drinking up the sky with their horses, made the ten directions shine with tiger-skins and golden moons."}},{"n":6,"text":"ते दंशिताः सुसंरब्धा रथैर्मेघौघनिस्वनैः ।\nसमावृण्वन्दिशः सर्वाः पार्थं च विशिखैः शितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Armoured and furious, with chariots that rumbled like masses of clouds, they covered all quarters and Partha with sharp arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"कौलूतका हयाश्चित्रा वहन्तस्तान्महारथान् ।\nव्यशोभन्त तदा शीघ्रा दीपयन्तो दिशो दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"The many-coloured Kauluta horses that bore those great chariot-warriors shone then, swift, lighting the ten directions."}},{"n":8,"text":"आजानेयैर्महावेगैर्नानादेशसमुत्थितैः ।\nपार्वतीयैर्नदीजैश्च सैन्धवैश्च हयोत्तमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were fast thoroughbreds from many lands, horses of the mountains, of the rivers, and the best Sindhu horses."}},{"n":9,"text":"कुरुयोधवरा राजंस्तव पुत्रं परीप्सवः ।\nधनंजयरथं शीघ्रं सर्वतः समुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The best Kuru warriors, O king, wishing to protect your son, rushed quickly from all sides at Dhananjaya's chariot."}},{"n":10,"text":"ते प्रगृह्य महाशङ्खान्दध्मुः पुरुषसत्तमाः ।\nपूरयन्तो दिवं राजन्पृथिवीं च ससागराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those best of men took up great conches and blew them, filling the sky and earth with its seas."}},{"n":11,"text":"तथैव दध्मतुः शङ्खौ वासुदेवधनंजयौ ।\nप्रवरौ सर्वभूतानां सर्वशङ्खवरौ भुवि ।\nदेवदत्तं च कौन्तेयः पाञ्चजन्यं च केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Likewise Vasudeva and Dhananjaya blew their conches, the foremost of all beings and best of all conches on earth: the Devadatta of Kunti's son, and the Panchajanya of Keshava."}},{"n":12,"text":"शब्दस्तु देवदत्तस्य धनंजयसमीरितः ।\nपृथिवीं चान्तरिक्षं च दिशश्चैव समावृणोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sound of the Devadatta, blown by Dhananjaya, filled earth, space and the quarters."}},{"n":13,"text":"तथैव पाञ्चजन्योऽपि वासुदेवसमीरितः ।\nसर्वशब्दानतिक्रम्य पूरयामास रोदसी ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too the Panchajanya, blown by Vasudeva, surpassed all sounds and filled heaven and earth."}},{"n":14,"text":"तस्मिंस्तथा वर्तमाने दारुणे नादसंकुले ।\nभीरूणां त्रासजनने शूराणां हर्षवर्धने ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that dreadful uproar was thus going on, which brought fear to the timid and joy to the brave,"}},{"n":15,"text":"प्रवादितासु भेरीषु झर्झरेष्वानकेषु च ।\nमृदङ्गेषु च राजेन्द्र वाद्यमानेष्वनेकशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and as kettledrums, cymbals, tabors and drums were sounded in many ways, O king of kings,"}},{"n":16,"text":"महारथसमाख्याता दुर्योधनहितैषिणः ।\nअमृष्यमाणास्तं शब्दं क्रुद्धाः परमधन्विनः ।\nनानादेश्या महीपालाः स्वसैन्यपरिरक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the kings of many lands, known as great chariot-warriors, well-wishers of Duryodhana, supreme bowmen, guarding their own armies, could not bear that sound and grew angry."}},{"n":17,"text":"अमर्षिता महाशङ्खान्दध्मुर्वीरा महारथाः ।\nकृते प्रतिकरिष्यन्तः केशवस्यार्जुनस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The heroic great chariot-warriors, impatient, blew their great conches, wishing to answer what Keshava and Arjuna had done."}},{"n":18,"text":"बभूव तव तत्सैन्यं शङ्खशब्दसमीरितम् ।\nउद्विग्नरथनागाश्वमस्वस्थमिव चाभिभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your army, stirred by the conch-sounds, grew disturbed, with its chariots, elephants and horses agitated, and was unsettled, my lord."}},{"n":19,"text":"तत्प्रयुक्तमिवाकाशं शूरैः शङ्खनिनादितम् ।\nबभूव भृशमुद्विग्नं निर्घातैरिव नादितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sky, as if filled by the brave and resounding with conches, became greatly disturbed, as if shaken by thunderclaps."}},{"n":20,"text":"स शब्दः सुमहान्राजन्दिशः सर्वा व्यनादयत् ।\nत्रासयामास तत्सैन्यं युगान्त इव संभृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great sound, O king, echoed through all the quarters and frightened that army, like the gathered din at the end of an age."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनोऽष्टौ च राजानस्ते महारथाः ।\nजयद्रथस्य रक्षार्थं पाण्डवं पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana and those eight kings, great chariot-warriors, surrounded the Pandava to protect Jayadratha."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततो द्रौणिस्त्रिसप्तत्या वासुदेवमताडयत् ।\nअर्जुनं च त्रिभिर्भल्लैर्ध्वजमश्वांश्च पञ्चभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son struck Vasudeva with seventy-three arrows, Arjuna with three broad arrows, and his banner and horses with five."}},{"n":23,"text":"तमर्जुनः पृषत्कानां शतैः षड्भिरताडयत् ।\nअत्यर्थमिव संक्रुद्धः प्रतिविद्धे जनार्दने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna struck him with six hundred arrows, as if greatly enraged that Janardana had been wounded in return."}},{"n":24,"text":"कर्णं द्वादशभिर्विद्ध्वा वृषसेनं त्रिभिस्तथा ।\nशल्यस्य सशरं चापं मुष्टौ चिच्छेद वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having pierced Karna with twelve and Vrishasena with three, the mighty one cut Shalya's bow with its arrow in his fist."}},{"n":25,"text":"गृहीत्वा धनुरन्यत्तु शल्यो विव्याध पाण्डवम् ।\nभूरिश्रवास्त्रिभिर्बाणैर्हेमपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking another bow, Shalya pierced the Pandava, and Bhurishravas pierced him with three gold-feathered arrows sharpened on stone."}},{"n":26,"text":"कर्णो द्वात्रिंशता चैव वृषसेनश्च पञ्चभिः ।\nजयद्रथस्त्रिसप्तत्या कृपश्च दशभिः शरैः ।\nमद्रराजश्च दशभिर्विव्यधुः फल्गुनं रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna with thirty-two, Vrishasena with five, Jayadratha with seventy-three, Kripa with ten, and the king of the Madras with ten, pierced Phalguna in the battle."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततः शराणां षष्ट्या तु द्रौणिः पार्थमवाकिरत् ।\nवासुदेवं च सप्तत्या पुनः पार्थं च पञ्चभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son covered Partha with sixty arrows, Vasudeva with seventy, and Partha again with five."}},{"n":28,"text":"प्रहसंस्तु नरव्याघ्रः श्वेताश्वः कृष्णसारथिः ।\nप्रत्यविध्यत्स तान्सर्वान्दर्शयन्पाणिलाघवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The white-horsed tiger among men with Krishna as his charioteer, laughing, struck back at them all, showing the lightness of his hand."}},{"n":29,"text":"कर्णं द्वादशभिर्विद्ध्वा वृषसेनं त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nशल्यस्य समरे चापं मुष्टिदेशे न्यकृन्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Karna with twelve arrows and Vrishasena with three, and cut Shalya's bow in the battle at the grip."}},{"n":30,"text":"सौमदत्तिं त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा शल्यं च दशभिः शरैः ।\nशितैरग्निशिखाकारैर्द्रौणिं विव्याध चाष्टभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Somadatta's son with three, Shalya with ten, and Drona's son with eight sharp arrows like tongues of fire."}},{"n":31,"text":"गौतमं पञ्चविंशत्या शैन्धवं च शतेन ह ।\nपुनर्द्रौणिं च सप्तत्या शराणां सोऽभ्यताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he struck Gautama with twenty-five, the Saindhava with a hundred, and again Drona's son with seventy arrows."}},{"n":32,"text":"भूरिश्रवास्तु संक्रुद्धः प्रतोदं चिच्छिदे हरेः ।\nअर्जुनं च त्रिसप्तत्या बाणानामाजघान ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, greatly enraged, cut Hari's whip, and struck Arjuna with seventy-three arrows."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततः शरशतैस्तीक्ष्णैस्तानरीञ्श्वेतवाहनः ।\nप्रत्यषेधद्द्रुतं क्रुद्धो महावातो घनानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the white-horsed Arjuna, angry, quickly held back those foes with hundreds of sharp arrows, as a great wind drives back clouds."}}]}]}